            <ArticleTitle>Direct parasitologial diagnosis of infection with Hysterothylacium aduncum in a patient with epigastralgia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>699-700</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anisakis parasitization has been on the rise because some factors, like increased interest in dishes consisting of raw fish. We report a case of epigastralgia with direct diagnosis by endoscopy, which futher study pointed out H. Aduncum as causal agent, a anisakis which is rarely involved in human anisakiasis.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
